  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">10th Annual Women in Policing Conference - 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2012, the annual Women in Policing Conference brings together police officers from various backgrounds into a professional network with the joint motivation for achievement of a gender-sensitive approach to security, safety, justice, and public order. The 10th annual conference will aim to gather an estimated number of 320 participants from up to 15 countries. It is scheduled to take place on 6-11 March 2023 in Tbilisi. The overall objective is to contribute to international efforts to mainstream gender in policing, including border policing, focusing on areas such as policy and oversight, technology and social media, community policing and crime reduction, training and education, and officer wellness and safety.</narrative>
  </description>
